    ("faq", dict(
        label="FAQ", title="Frequently asked questions", icon="help",
        desc="Answers to the questions administrators ask most",
        keywords=["faq", "questions", "help", "how do i", "license", "redis", "backup", "upgrade", "migrate", "nexus", "artifactory", "air-gapped", "password", "locked out"],
        blocks=[
            H("Licensing"),
            UL([
                "**How do I get a license?** Read the installation ID (setup wizard, Settings → Application → Licensing, or `./server --machine-id`) and send it through [vectored.dev/#contact](https://vectored.dev/#contact) or to " + SUPPORT_MAIL + ". See [Get a license](licensing.html#get-a-license).",
                "**What happens when the license expires?** Any grace period first, with banners; then only sign-in, health checks and the license page answer, until a new license is applied. Nothing is deleted. See [When a license expires](licensing.html#when-a-license-expires).",
                "**We moved Depotex to new servers and it wants a new license.** The installation ID follows the machine (on Kubernetes, the pod's identity). Request a license for the new ID before moving, and apply it on the recovery page.",
                "**Does applying a license need a restart?** No, it applies at once. Some features notice a change of tier only after a restart.",
                "**Does Depotex call home?** No. It doesn't need internet access to check its license. It sends the installation ID only when it downloads the vibe artifacts package list (Enterprise, off without an address).",
            ]),
            H("Installation"),
            UL([
                "**Do I need Redis?** Not for a single server. A cluster needs it. See [Single Node & Cluster](deployment-modes.html).",
                "**Which PostgreSQL?** 15 or later; managed services work. The role must own the database and needn't be a superuser.",
                "**Can it run without internet access?** Yes. Mirror the images, use Depotex or internal mirrors as upstreams, and upload vulnerability data offline (Settings → Vulnerability data).",
                "**Can I run it under a path such as /depotex?** No, it needs its own host name.",
                "**Can I set it up with no browser?** Yes, from a YAML file: [Set up without the UI](headless-setup.html).",
                "**Where is the Helm chart?** The published chart location is TBD; see [Install with Helm](helm-chart.html).",
                "**How do I move from Nexus or Artifactory?** Create proxy repositories on your old server as an upstream to switch builds without downtime, then publish your hosted packages to Depotex with each format's client. Ask [support](support.html) for help planning a migration.",
            ]),
            H("Access"),
            UL([
                "**I'm locked out: single sign-on is down.** Start one server with `SSO_ENFORCEMENT_OVERRIDE=true`, sign in with a password as a super admin, fix the provider, then remove the variable.",
                "**An account is locked after failed sign-ins.** It unlocks after `AUTH_LOCKOUT_DURATION` (15 minutes), or a super admin unlocks it in Settings → Access → Users.",
                "**A super admin forgot their password.** Another super admin resets it. If no one can sign in, use **Forgot password** with email configured, or contact [support](support.html).",
                "**How do I give CI access without a person's token?** A service account with an OAuth application, or workload identity with no secret at all. See [OAuth Applications](oauth-applications.html).",
                "**Why does everyone seem to come from the same address?** `TRUSTED_PROXIES` doesn't include your proxy. See [Behind a proxy](install.html#behind-a-proxy).",
            ]),
            H("Data"),
            UL([
                "**What's in a backup?** The database (settings, people, repositories' records) and platform files (logos, avatars, plugin packages), not artifacts. Protect artifact storage with your storage platform. See [Backups](backups.html).",
                "**I lost CONFIG_ENCRYPTION_KEY.** Stored credentials and backups made with it can't be read; there is no recovery. Keep the key in a secret store and with your backup records.",
                "**How do I reclaim disk space?** Cleanup policies per space, quotas, emptying the trash, and Docker garbage collection (automatic). See [Spaces](spaces.html).",
                "**Can a deleted repository be restored?** Yes, for 7 days by default: Settings → Repositories → Deleted repositories.",
            ]),
            H("Operations"),
            UL([
                "**How do I upgrade without downtime?** Run a cluster and upgrade one server at a time. See [Upgrades & maintenance](upgrades.html).",
                "**The system check warns about Live updates.** Route `/api/ws` to the server with WebSocket upgrades allowed.",
                "**How do I see what a server is doing?** Settings → Logging: levels per area, log files, exports and profiles; Settings → Advanced → Scheduled jobs for background work.",
                "**How do I hear about security fixes?** Subscribe to the [security advisory feed](security-advisories.html).",
            ]),
        ])),

